The custom graph matrix agrees with the archived pyMARS implementation within 1.78e-15 absolute error; the maximum-product paths agree with an independent Floyd closure within 1.11e-16. Reactor temperature/pressure derivatives agree with a short integration-step check within 3.3e-5 relative error. These checks validate implementation components, not the physical accuracy of the reaction mechanism.

## Final parent-fidelity validation

Before candidate results, the strict limits were set at **10% maximum ignition-delay error and 5% maximum flame-speed error**. The compact limits were **20% and 10%**. The strict tier aims to keep added structural error small on the scale of common ignition and flame measurement uncertainty; the compact tier explicitly trades more error for a smaller state vector and reaction network. These are exploratory engineering tolerances, distinct from each observation's reported uncertainty. Error is `100 × abs(reduced/parent − 1)`. A missing, failed or nonigniting case cannot pass. Median and 95th-percentile errors describe typical performance but cannot erase a maximum violation.

