All 102 development and all 51 independent confirmation cases succeed for every model. The strict candidates meet 10%/5%; the compact candidate meets 20%/10%. These are errors against the parent, not against experiments. The complete [fidelity table](results/final_fidelity/summary.csv) and [point records](results/final_fidelity/details.csv) retain signed errors and limiting case IDs. The [accuracy–complexity figure](figures/complexity_tradeoff.svg) distinguishes coarse screening from final refined development results.

The three YAML files were frozen at **2026-09-15 20:45:48 UTC**, before any of this run's external prediction errors or reduced-model confirmation results were inspected. High and balanced external jobs had been queued with byte-identical source candidates; their hashes are recorded in `raw/external_precompute_pins.json`. No chemistry was revised after inspecting these comparisons. The 51 confirmation conditions were fixed before reduction and differ from the development conditions in temperature, pressure and equivalence ratio. All three retained their declared tolerances on this separate set; no missing or failed confirmation case was excluded. The largest confirmation ignition errors occur for butadiene in 93/553 and 88/475 and acetylene in 74/433; the largest flame errors occur for n-butane, acetylene and butadiene, respectively.

